# 1. Purpose

Perform a complete independent review of the final SpeedReader Production Package before it is allowed to become an authoritative deployable artifact.

Stage 05 QA determines whether the production package:

- contains only independently approved upstream artifacts;
- preserves approved learner-facing content exactly;
- preserves approved assessment meaning and scoring exactly;
- maintains correct World/Band/RS/P/delivery identity;
- satisfies the production/runtime schema;
- contains complete traceability and provenance;
- introduces no unauthorized transformation;
- contains no dependency on WIP artifacts;
- correctly separates learner-facing and internal information;
- can be safely handed to the deployment/integration pipeline.

Stage 05 QA reviews and certifies.

It must not create, rewrite or repair upstream content.

---

# 2. Fundamental Gate Rule

No Production Package may leave the content pipeline unless Stage 05 QA returns:

```text
PASS
```

for the exact package artifact reviewed.

The following are insufficient:

```text
